# Project layout

Trenches, Guns and Magic (TGM). Before edits, searches, or new files, map where material belongs and read the closest existing file in that area.

## Root

- `README.md`: project title only.
- `System.md`: tooling and workflow notes.
- `Status.md`: live protagonist sheet (Maximilian Friedrich); stats, gear, kills, magic, system state.
- `LICENSE`: license text.

## `Story/`

Working narrative chapters. Numbered `01.md` through `13.md`, plus `01.5.md`. New chapter prose belongs here unless the task names another path.

## `Source/`

Upstream novel material: numbered chapter files (currently through `480.md`) and bulk `.txt` sources. Reference for continuity and wording; do not treat as the edited manuscript.

## `References/`

Canon and editorial references. Verify names, places, gear, magic, and military detail here before changing `Story/` or `Status.md`. Index: `Reference-Files-Catalog.md`.

- `Editorial/`: prose mechanics, editor contract.
- `Setting/`: glossary, world and setting framework.
- `Geography/`: countries, places, theaters, locations and resources.
- `Characters/`: people, dynastic notes, character sheet, aides.
- `Magic-and-Systems/`: magic rules, Max system mechanics.
- `Military/`: armies, weapons, armor, German kit and doctrine.
- `Biology-and-Chemistry/`: engineered biology, substances, Lilyvitae.
- `Planning/`: alternate history drafts, notes for the future, villain bible.
- `Society/`: religions and denominations.
- `Regional/`: cultural regions, flora and fauna, food, Japan actions.

## `Tools/`

Automation only (`people-localize.ps1`, `run-people-localize.ps1`, `people-name-replacements.json`). Do not store fiction or reference notes here.

## `.cursor/rules/`

Persistent agent rules for this repo.

## Placement

- Fiction and chapter drafts: `Story/`.
- Worldbuilding, style, and fact sheets: `References/`.
- Raw or upstream chapters: `Source/`.
- Character or system state tracking: `Status.md`.
- Scripts and replacement data: `Tools/`.

When a task spans folders, read `Story/` for the current draft, `Source/` for upstream wording, `References/` for canon, and `Status.md` for present state before editing.
